;; The real race (race.yml, clojure -M:race): each lane carries servers on one of the pregenerated
;; landing sets, each server its own race process and bots. Which start a lane plays and the page
;; its results go under are in ci/lanes.edn; what a start is, in resources/clojurecraft/starts.edn.
{:race/runners 8 ; GitHub runners
 :race/servers 1 ; servers per runner, each its own world copy, race process and bots: one ticks 2-5x faster than two sharing the runner's two cores
 :race/landing-sets ["R1" "R2" "R3" "R4"] ; ci/gym.edn's race worlds: runner r races on set (r-1) mod 4
 :race/bots 10 ; bot slots per server, each refilled the moment its bot ends
 :race/prefix "Clj_r" ; bot names: Clj_r01, Clj_r02, ... one serial per server for the job
 :race/until "pearls-12" ; the target; a bot plays every step from its start up to it (plan/through)
 :race/run-minutes 330 ; how long each runner plays, near GitHub's 6 h job cap
 :race/stagger-ms 3000 ; between bots joining a server
 :race/server-heap-mb 6144 ; each server's JVM
 :race/bot-heap-mb 2048 ; each race process's JVM
 ;; per server (by --server k): settings over clojurecraft.servers/defaults (simulation distance 3)
 :race/server-overrides {}
 ;; per lane (race.yml's runner): race keys over this file's own. An A/B of bots a server: lanes
 ;; 1 3 6 8 carry 14 bots (with a bigger race heap), the others 10, so each start (ci/lanes.edn:
 ;; rods 1-4, forest 5-8) and each landing set (lane r on set (r-1) mod 4) has both arms. Lanes on
 ;; a set are landing-stride apart, the most landings any lane takes, so none overlap
 :race/lane-overrides {1 {:race/bots 14 :race/bot-heap-mb 3072}
                       3 {:race/bots 14 :race/bot-heap-mb 3072}
                       6 {:race/bots 14 :race/bot-heap-mb 3072}
                       8 {:race/bots 14 :race/bot-heap-mb 3072}}}
